ncrete scenario can map it to their own situation. An abstract rule doesn't give them that bridge.\n\n5. **They settle arguments.** \"That won't work\" meets \"Here's where it did\" — the example wins every time because reality beats speculation.\n\nIn short: **abstractions tell you what *could* be true; examples show what *is* true.** The best thinking uses both — example first to ground the idea, then abstraction to extend it."}]},"duplicate_hook_observation_count":0,"duplicate_dream_suppressed_count":0}
